# A compiled Rill program has no extension and lands next to its source — in
# the project root by default, and in every chapter of the book. Nothing that
# belongs in this repository is extensionless, so that is the rule: a file with
# no dot in its name is something a build left behind. Add an exception here if
# a LICENSE or a Makefile ever needs to go in.
*
!*/
!*.*

# Directories were all taken back on the second line above, so the ones that
# are build output or cache have to be named again — the last rule that
# matches is the one that counts.
/target/
/benchmarks/bin/
node_modules/

# The Windows SDK, fetched once with `xwin` for cross-compilation. A gigabyte,
# and not ours to redistribute.
/.xwin-cache/

# The packaged toolchain; `tools/dist.sh` rebuilds it.
/dist/

# Local, per-machine settings.
/.claude/

# Build output that does have an extension.
*.o
*.wasm
*.vsix
.DS_Store

# Generated by book/make-pdf.sh from the chapter files. `assemble.py` and
# `head.tex` sit in the same directory and are its inputs, so they stay.
/book/build/book.md
/book/build/rill.pdf

# A 24 MB application archive that nothing on the site links to. Kept out of
# history deliberately — the file is untouched on disk, and deleting this line
# puts it back. `site/rill.pdf`, which index.html does link, stays in.
/site/*.zip

# The valley server writes the names people gave it, beside itself. It is a
# running program leaving state where it stands, and a local test creates one.
/examples/webgpu/world/who.txt

# The asset bundle is written by pack.rill from the files beside it — the
# deploy rsyncs it from the working directory and the repo keeps the sources.
*.rpak

# The page, concatenated and then minified — both written by the packer and
# build.sh out of world.js, net.js, host.js and boot.js, which are the files
# that are actually edited and tracked.
/examples/webgpu/world/page.js
/examples/webgpu/world/page.min.js
